Migration setup
===============

Revisions are the single source of truth for schema. The initial revision is an explicit DDL snapshot; the application no longer creates tables from model metadata at startup. On startup the app runs `upgrade head` and then writes idempotent seed data. For production deployments, run migrations with the same DATABASE_URL used by the application:

  alembic upgrade head

When changing model definitions, generate and review a new migration before applying it:

  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

A database without `alembic_version`, or with a revision outside this chain, is rejected at startup. Back up and verify the schema first; if it matches head, run `alembic stamp head`.
